From: Stefano Castagnetta <scastagnetta@nvidia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] [PR #60068] [MRV2][Spec Decode] Opt-in confidence stop for autoregressive drafting

Upstream-PR: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60068
Upstream-Commit: 8ae78ccaf8825b3e55ab014e282c769902ca198c
Integration-Base: 564ac0de1b228568cafcbfbe8ccaccc82d6023eb
Refresh-Base: 790be385c8a69f45ec9a7a85ef00836d1684060f

Preserve both quantized draft-head and adaptive-depth documentation/tests.
Use #60692's supports_decode_metadata_update API; confidence stopping
requires a separate graph for each draft step. Preserve the upstream
watermarked sampling branch and update confidence before either sampler
can modify logits in place.

Retain upstream DraftLogitsCache and target attention-metadata reuse.

Preserve upstream decode_graph_eligible when dispatching adaptive draft batches.

Use the shared autoregressive decode loop and config-level graph shape mapping.

